PR #268 - changes required
1. [BLOCKER] frontend/src/components/ThreadOdometer.tsx:25 - The counter's only accessible text is supplied via `aria-label` on a plain `<span>` while the visible value is `aria-hidden="true"`. A generic span has no implicit ARIA role, so assistive technology is not required to expose or announce that label; in practice this can leave the calls/token/cost counters silent (the test only checks the raw attribute, not the accessibility tree). Give the counter an appropriate exposed role (for example `role="img"` if it is purely informational) or include a visually-hidden text node and verify it with an accessibility-oriented regression test. Apply the same consideration to the aggregate `aria-label="Thread usage"` span in `frontend/src/pages/ThreadPage.tsx:208`.

